{number: 156}
{title: Fill My Cup, Lord}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Like the woman at the well I was [F7] seeking
For things that could not satis-[Bb] fy;
And then I heard my Savior [Eb] speaking:
“Draw from My [Bb] well that [F7] never shall run [Bb] dry.”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Fill my [Bb] cup, Lord, I lift it [F7] up, Lord!
Come and quench this thirsting of my [Bb] soul;
Bread of [Bb] heaven, feed me till I [Eb] want no more,
Fill my [Bb] cup, fill it [F7] up and make me [Bb] whole!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There [Bb] are millions in this world who are [F7] craving
The pleasure earthly things af-[Bb] ford;
But none can match the wondrous [Eb] treasure
That I [Bb] find in [F7] Jesus Christ my [Bb] Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
So, [Bb] my brother, if the things this world [F7] gave you
Leave hungers that won't pass a-[Bb] way,
My blessed Lord will come and [Eb] save you,
If you [Bb] kneel to [F7] Him and humbly [Bb] pray.
{end_of_verse}
